graph=3D""><strong class=3D"no hm"><em class=3D"ol">=E2=80=9CPre-trained=E2=
=80=9D</em></strong> implies the use of tranfer learning. If you=E2=80=99re=
 not familiar with transfer learning, it usually goes like this:</p><ol cla=
ss=3D""><li id=3D"8ece" class=3D"nm nn hl no b np nq nr ns nt nu nv nw nx n=
y nz oa ob oc od oe of og oh oi oj om on oo bl" data-selectable-paragraph=
=3D"">First, a gigantic, generalized language model is trained on a huge am=
ount of data</li><li id=3D"e556" class=3D"nm nn hl no b np op nr ns nt oq n=
v nw nx or nz oa ob os od oe of ot oh oi oj om on oo bl" data-selectable-pa=
ragraph=3D"">Then, this model is fine-tuned (trained briefly) to perform so=
me specific task.</li></ol><p id=3D"5dce" class=3D"pw-post-body-paragraph n=
m nn hl no b np nq nr ns nt nu nv nw nx ny nz oa ob oc od oe of og oh oi oj=
 he bl" data-selectable-paragraph=3D"">Lastly, <strong class=3D"no hm"><em =
class=3D"ol">=E2=80=9CTransformer=E2=80=9D</em></strong> is referring to th=
e Transformer architecture. This architecture was first introduced in a pap=
er called <em class=3D"ol">Attention Is All You Need</em> (2017), which <a =
class=3D"ah ok" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1706.03762.pdf" rel=3D"noopen=
er ugc nofollow" target=3D"_blank">can be found here</a>. This paper has be=
come one of the most consequential (and cited) in the history of AI.</p><p =
id=3D"ad2e" class=3D"pw-post-body-paragraph nm nn hl no b np nq nr ns nt nu=
 nv nw nx ny nz oa ob oc od oe of og oh oi oj he bl" data-selectable-paragr=
aph=3D"">In this post, we=E2=80=99ll take a closer look at the underlying a=
rchitecture of the Transformer, and what makes it so powerful.</p><p id=3D"=
