C%20Transformers%2C%20and%20GPT.ipynb" rel=3D"noopener ugc nofollow" target=
=3D"_blank">found here</a>.</p><h2 id=3D"ab86" class=3D"ou ov hl bg ow ox o=
y oz pa pb pc pd pe pf pg ph pi pj pk pl pm pn po pp pq pr bl" data-selecta=
ble-paragraph=3D"">The Attention Mechanism</h2><p id=3D"9200" class=3D"pw-p=
ost-body-paragraph nm nn hl no b np ps nr ns nt pt nv nw nx pu nz oa ob pv =
od oe of pw oh oi oj he bl" data-selectable-paragraph=3D"">At the heart of =
the Transformer architecture is the Attention mechanism, introduced in a pa=
per called <a class=3D"ah ok" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1409.0473.pdf" =
rel=3D"noopener ugc nofollow" target=3D"_blank"><em class=3D"ol">Neural Mac=
hine Translation By Jointly Learning to Align and Translate</em>, by Bahdan=
au et al</a>. It is a sequence-to-sequence operation; meaning, a sequence o=
f vectors goes in, and a sequence of vectors comes out. So, although origin=
ally designed for machine translation, it can be applied to any task involv=
ing sequential data.</p><p id=3D"3596" class=3D"pw-post-body-paragraph nm n=
n hl no b np nq nr ns nt nu nv nw nx ny nz oa ob oc od oe of og oh oi oj he=
 bl" data-selectable-paragraph=3D"">There are many variations of Attention,=
 but we=E2=80=99ll be focusing on the flavor defined in <a class=3D"ah ok" =
href=3D"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1706.03762.pdf" rel=3D"noopener ugc nofollow"=
 target=3D"_blank"><em class=3D"ol">Attention Is All You Need</em></a>. Her=
e, the authors define attention in the following way:</p><blockquote class=
=3D"px py pz"><p id=3D"f850" class=3D"nm nn ol no b np nq nr ns nt nu nv nw=
 nx ny nz oa ob oc od oe of og oh oi oj he bl" data-selectable-paragraph=3D=
"">=E2=80=9CAn attention function can be described as mapping a query and a=
 set of key-value pairs to an output, where the query, keys, values, and ou=
tput are all vectors. The output is computed as a weighted sum of the value=
s, where the weight assigned to each value is computed by a compatibility f=
unction of the query with the corresponding key.=E2=80=9D</p></blockquote><=
p id=3D"9c24" class=3D"pw-post-body-paragraph nm nn hl no b np nq nr ns nt =
nu nv nw nx ny nz oa ob oc od oe of og oh oi oj he bl" data-selectable-para=
graph=3D"">The attention mechanism described in the paper is called <em cla=
ss=3D"ol">Scaled Dot-Product Attention</em>, and is defined as the below:</=
